meta {
  name: Chat completion
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{URL}}/openai/v1/chat/completions
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer paste-virtual-key-here
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "model": "gpt-4o",
    "messages": [
      { "role": "user", "content": "Say hello in five words." }
    ],
    "max_tokens": 64
  }
}

settings {
  encodeUrl: true
}

docs {
  The gateway route. `/openai` names the inbound wire format, not the upstream —
  the `model` field decides where the request actually goes.

  A bare name like `gpt-4o` draws across the providers on the key. Pin one with
  `openai/gpt-4o` to skip the draw.

  Requires, in order: a virtual key, a budget with headroom, the model allowed on
  the key, and a live credential on the chosen provider. Each failure has its own
  status — 401 no key, 403 model not permitted, 429 budget exhausted.
}
